Package: decisionpaths
Title: Construct and Audit Longitudinal Decision Paths
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(
      given   = "Subir",
      family  = "Hait",
      role    = c("aut", "cre"),
      email   = "haitsubi@msu.edu",
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-9871-9677")
    )
Description: Tools for constructing and auditing longitudinal decision paths
    from panel data. Provides functions to represent repeated institutional
    decisions as path objects, summarize path descriptors (dosage, switching,
    onset, duration), compute the Decision Reliability Index (DRI) grounded
    in classical test theory (Cronbach, 1951; Nunnally, 1978), estimate
    Shannon decision-path entropy (Shannon, 1948), classify infrastructure
    type (static, periodically recalibrated, continuously adaptive,
    human-in-the-loop), and evaluate subgroup disparities via standardized
    mean differences. Implements the decision infrastructure paradigm
    introduced in Hait (2025), with applications in education, policy,
    health, and organizational research.
